# A white page under dark websites gets a white bar. Since engine 159.0.8154.13-16 a page's view shows Arc's
# canvas (black while websites are dark) until the page's first frame, and the load-end capture the bar's colour
# comes from (#629) could land before that frame: the bar read black over a white page and kept it until a reload.
# The 0.1.55 release's toolbar snapshots caught it on a Mac in Dark mode. View ▸ Appearance ▸ Dark makes websites
# dark here whatever the Mac is set to. The sampler reads again while it sees only the canvas (ToolbarSample).
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": true}
cra://action/appearanceDark
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first
wait 4
cra://debug?toolbarColor=first
expect-log toolbar colour first: bar=FFFFFF$
cra://action/reload
wait 4
cra://debug?toolbarColor=reloaded
expect-log toolbar colour reloaded: bar=FFFFFF$
# A page whose own top is black keeps a black bar: only the canvas is read again.
cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/toolbar-dark.html
wait 4
cra://debug?toolbarColor=dark
expect-log toolbar colour dark: bar=0D1117$
cra://action/appearanceAutomatic
